# Nothing under resources/ is ever committed.
#
# It holds Apple's firmware and ROM dumps, the shipping game binaries, multi-gigabyte disk images,
# and cloned reference sources (Rockbox, ipodloader2, wInd3x, ghidra-mcp). Copyrighted material and
# large binaries both, either of which is reason enough on its own.
#
# tools/ipod-boot/README.md documents the layout under resources/derived/ and which of those files
# cannot be regenerated.
#
# The repository root also ignores this path. Keeping a copy here means the rule travels with the
# project rather than depending on where it sits.
#
# Both forms deliberately. A trailing slash matches a directory ONLY — an agent working in a git
# worktree symlinks `resources` in to run the recipes, and a symlink is not a directory, so it
# appeared as untracked and was one `git add -A` from being committed. The material behind it is
# copyrighted reference data plus real people's names and Apple IDs; it must never enter history.
resources
resources/

.DS_Store

# Emulator run output — framebuffer dumps, profiles. Regenerable; never review-relevant.
_out/

# Per-agent cargo target dirs and audit scratch — regenerable, never review-relevant.
.target-*/
.audit/

# Per-agent / scratch build dirs
.t/
.target-*/

# Release archives, staged by .github/workflows/release.yml or by hand when Actions cannot run.
dist/

# The release checklist is the operator's, not the reader's. Kept on disk, out of the tree.
RELEASING.md
